# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# gifsy-posm FRONTEND (Next.js 16) — STAGING (Cloud Run service `posm-frontend-staging`)
#
# PLACEHOLDERS ONLY. Not loaded by the container: [build-arg] values are passed to
# `docker build --build-arg` in CI; [runtime] values are Cloud Run service env.
#   [secret] = Secret Manager (`--set-secrets`)   [plain] = ordinary env var
# NEVER commit a real .env.staging. Inventory: docs/plans/DEPLOY-ENV-VARS.md
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# [build-arg] The staging API service URL (no trailing slash). Baked in at BUILD time:
# next.config.ts rewrites `/api/*` → `${NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL}/v1/*`. Changing it requires a rebuild.
NEXT_PUBLIC_API_URL="https://<posm-api-staging Cloud Run URL>"

# [build-arg] Tenant (Client) the field login belongs to, inlined into the client bundle.
# ⚠️ The code sends this value as the backend `clientId` on send-otp/verify-otp, so it must be the
# seeded Kwality Client's id in the `posm_staging` DB. The deploy contract names it `kwality`;
# confirm that equals the real Client id (local dev uses a cuid) or login fails "not configured".
NEXT_PUBLIC_CLIENT_ID=kwality

# [runtime][secret] Secret Manager: `posm-staging-jwt-secret`.
# ⚠️ MUST BE IDENTICAL to the staging API's JWT_SECRET — the Next proxy (src/proxy.ts) verifies the
# api-issued tokens with it. A mismatch = every request redirects to login. The app throws on boot
# in production if this is unset.
JWT_SECRET="<from Secret Manager: posm-staging-jwt-secret>"

# [build-arg] Set by CI = the git SHA being deployed. Becomes Next's build id and
# NEXT_PUBLIC_BUILD_ID (the `/version` route + UpdateNudge stale-tab detection). Never hand-set.
BUILD_ID="<GIT_SHA — set by CI>"

# [plain] Production build mode (Cloud Run). PORT is injected by Cloud Run — do not set.
NODE_ENV=production
